      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n## Implemented behavior\n\nportDeclarations combines authored and synthetic declarations; graphNodeContract resolves Port presentation and glyphs. Graph navigation resolves an explicit exposed Port before falling back to the graph’s root landing behavior.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nUnifying Port presentation with Declaration Surfaces is not part of the current contract. Legacy inline presentation is readable but not a new authoring recommendation. See github://twilite-zone/public/tasks/declaration-surfaces/root.node.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/portRelationshipHandles.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/portDeclarations.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/graphNodeContract.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/graphNavigationAddress.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/portDeclarations.test.js`\n- `tests/dynamicPortDeclarations.test.js`\n- `tests/graphNavigationAddress.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port",
          "nodeId": "port-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
